  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nExpression = 9 1/6 × 4 2/3 + 5 1/2 ÷ 2 2/3\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nMixed fraction multiplication: a b/c = (a*c + b)/c\n\nMixed fraction division: a b/c ÷ d e/f = (a*c + b)/c ÷ (d*f + e)/f\n\n**Calculations:**\n\n9 1/6 = (9×6 + 1)/6 = 55/6\n\n4 2/3 = (4×3 + 2)/3 = 14/3\n\n5 1/2 = (5×2 + 1)/2 = 11/2\n\n2 2/3 = (2×3 + 2)/3 = 8/3\n\nNow, solving the expression:\n\nFirst, 9 1/6 × 4 2/3 = 55/6 × 14/3\n\n⇒ (55 × 14) / (6 × 3) = 770 / 18 = 385 / 9\n\nNext, 5 1/2 ÷ 2 2/3 = 11/2 ÷ 8/3\n\n⇒ (11 / 2) × (3 / 8) = 33 / 16\n\nNow, adding the results:\n\n385 / 9 + 33 / 16\n\nLCM of 9 and 16 = 144\n\n⇒ (385 × 16) / 144 + (33 × 9) / 144 = 6160 / 144 + 297 / 144\n\n⇒ 6457 / 144\n\n**∴ The value of the expression is 6457 / 144**",
